title: Lenalidomide - adverse effects and precautions
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

In [[multiple myeloma|Multiple myeloma]], prevent pregnancy/thrombosis and monitor cytopenias.

!! Most serious / long-term effects

|!Toxicity/complication|!Precaution or action|
|Venous/arterial thrombosis|Risk increases with dexamethasone. [[IMPEDE|IMPEDE VTE score]]/[[SAVED|SAVED score]]: aspirin for lower risk; anticoagulant prophylaxis for higher risk. Consider bleeding, platelets, renal function, interactions. New dyspnea/chest pain/unilateral swelling: urgent assessment.|
|Embryo-fetal toxicity|Pregnancy contraindicated. Risk Evaluation and Mitigation Strategy (REMS): pregnancy-testing, contraception, condoms, blood/sperm donation restrictions.|
|Severe skin reactions/hypersensitivity|Permanently discontinue for blistering/exfoliative rash, severe systemic skin reactions, or severe hypersensitivity.|
|Second primary malignancies|Increased risk, especially after melphalan (confounding?); maintenance benefits generally outweigh risk.|

!! Dose-limiting toxicities

|!Toxicity|!Management|
|Neutropenia, thrombocytopenia, anemia|Monitor blood counts; interrupt/reduce dosing for significant toxicity. Fever/bleeding: urgent assessment.|
|Persistent diarrhea|Exclude infection/other causes; consider bile-acid malabsorption and colesevelam.|
|Rash|<ul><li>Mild: antihistamines/topical steroids.</li><li>Moderate: consider interruption.</li><li>Severe: consider interruption; permanently discontinue for blistering/exfoliative or severe systemic reactions (see above).</li></ul>|

!! Other common and less common toxicities

|!Frequency|!Toxicity/precaution|
|Common|<ul><li>Fatigue</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Nausea</li><li>Muscle cramps</li><li>Edema</li><li>Diarrhea and rash: see above.</li></ul>|
|Less common|<ul><li>Hepatotoxicity: monitor liver enzymes.</li><li>Thyroid dysfunction: monitor thyroid function.</li><li>Peripheral neuropathy: less prominent than with thalidomide/bortezomib.</li></ul>|
|Impaired stem cell mobilization|Prolonged exposure can impair collection; plan early.|

''Dosing precaution:'' Renally cleared; monitor renal function and adjust dosing to creatinine clearance/treatment setting.

Sources: [[Merz 2020|https://doi.org/10.1007/s00277-020-04023-4]]; [[van de Donk 2012|https://doi.org/10.2147/CMAR.S27087]]; [[Delforge 2017|https://doi.org/10.1182/blood-2017-01-725705]]; [[Ludwig 2018|https://doi.org/10.1038/s41375-018-0040-1]]; [[GoodRx|https://www.goodrx.com/lenalidomide/common-side-effects]]; [[IMF|https://www.myeloma.org/revlimid-lenalidomide]]; [[US label, 3/2023, §§2,5|https://packageinserts.bms.com/pi/pi_revlimid.pdf]]; NCCN Multiple Myeloma v1.2027 (9/9/2026), MYEL-L 1–3, Discussion MS-25,63; ASH SAP 9th ed., ch.48, p.620; ASCO SEP 2026, ch.21, p.1220.
